a=r'''1.1 (Shuffle decomposition and freeness.) Choose reduced PBW words adapted to the parabolic subgroup $S_{|\beta|}\times S_{|\gamma|}$. For each concatenated word $\xi=\nu\ast\eta$ and minimal right coset representative $w$, the vectors $\tau_we(\xi)b$, with $b$ ranging through the PBW basis of $e(\xi)B$, form precisely the PBW basis of the right $B$-module $Ae$: the permutation is a minimal shuffle followed by an internal block permutation, with additive length, and the right idempotent records the source word in the corner $e$. Thus $Ae\cong\bigoplus_{w,\xi}e(\xi)B\{\delta_R(w,\xi)\}$, with the displayed degree of $\tau_we(\xi)$. Reversal of products fixing dots, crossings and idempotents preserves the defining relations and is an anti-involution; it sends $Ae$ to $eA$ and $\tau_we(\xi)$ to $e(\xi)\tau_{w^{-1}}$, giving the left $B$-module decomposition of $eA$ into the corresponding $Be(\xi)$ with shifts $\delta_L(w,\xi)=\deg(e(\xi)\tau_w)$. Both decompositions are finite sums of principal graded projectives. Ungraded, for each shuffle the sum over all concatenated $\xi$ is one copy of $B$, so both ranks are $\binom{|\beta|+|\gamma|}{|\beta|}$. Neither bimodule is replaced by $eAe$: its unconstrained opposite endpoint is essential for the shuffle basis. [given, F1, algebra]'''
b=r'''2.1 (Exactness and projectivity.) The right $B$-module $Ae$ is projective, hence flat, by step 1.1, so $\mathrm{Ind}=Ae\otimes_B-$ is exact by [F2]. Idempotent restriction is exact on left modules: for a surjection $L\to N$, a vector $en\in eN$ lifts to $e\ell\in eL$, and kernels and images commute with multiplication by the degree-zero idempotent $e$; no right action on $L$ is required. A finitely generated graded projective left $B$-module is a summand of a finite sum of shifts of $B$, so its induction is a summand of the corresponding sum of shifts of $Ae$. As a left $A$-module $Ae$ is the image of the degree-zero idempotent endomorphism $a\mapsto ae$ of $A$, hence is finitely generated graded projective. Similarly, if $P$ is a finitely generated graded projective left $A$-module, realize $P$ as a summand of a finite sum of shifts of $A$ and apply $e(-)$ to its split inclusion and projection. Then $eP$ is a summand of the corresponding sum of shifts of $eA$, which is finitely generated graded projective as a left $B$-module by step 1.1. Internal shifts commute with induction and restriction because their balance relations and idempotent action have degree zero. This proves exactness, shift compatibility and both finite-projective preservation clauses. [step 1.1, F2, F4, algebra]'''
